{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable events) from motion (controllable events). The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: move forward or random_walk in clear, recover with directed turns or backward motion when obstacles are detected, and only use full_rotate as a last-resort scan after repeated blockages. All obstacle events force recovery states, and the robot returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton binds sensor outcomes to safe, coverage-biased actions, ensuring recovery after obstacles and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
